===Szechuan Sauce===
Szechuan Sauce, or Mulan Sauce, was a dipping sauce for chicken nuggets created to promote the 1998 Disney film ''[[Mulan (1998 film)|Mulan]]''.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Kim|first1=Jae-Ha|date=June 21, 1998|title=Beyond Asian stereotypes|url=http://www.jaehakim.com/lifestyles/issue-lifestyles/beyond-asian-stereotypes/|url-status=live|newspaper=[[Chicago Sun-Times]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170622210218/http://www.jaehakim.com/lifestyles/issue-lifestyles/beyond-asian-stereotypes/|archive-date=June 22, 2017|access-date=October 16, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite journal|last1=Gibson|first1=Richard|last2=Orwall|first2=Bruce|date=March 5, 1998|title=New Mission for Mickey Mouse, Mickey D|journal=[[The Wall Street Journal]]|page=B1|quote=For 'Mulan,' the chain is contemplating serving plum or Szechwan sauce with its Chicken McNuggets.}}</ref> The sauce was sold for a limited time, starting on June 16, 1998.<ref>{{cite journal|last1=Har|first1=Janie|date=June 19, 1998|title=Movie tie-in holds nugget of debate|journal=[[Scripps Howard News Service]]|quote=Both the Chicken McNuggets, offered with a "Szechwan" dipping sauce, and "Mulan" Happy Meals debuted Tuesday.}}</ref> Szechuan Sauce returned to the cultural spotlight almost twenty years later after being referenced numerous times in "[[The Rickshank Rickdemption]]", the [[Rick and Morty (season 3)|Season 3]] premiere of the [[Adult Swim]] animated comedy ''[[Rick and Morty]]''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.polygon.com/tv/2017/8/7/16107724/rick-and-morty-szechuan-sauce-auction|title=Rick and Morty fans are bidding more than $4,500 on Szechuan sauce (update)|last1=Alexander|first1=Julia|website=[[Polygon (website)|Polygon]]|date=August 7, 2017|publisher=August 14, 2017|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171003132606/https://www.polygon.com/tv/2017/8/7/16107724/rick-and-morty-szechuan-sauce-auction|archive-date=October 3, 2017|access-date=October 6, 2017}}</ref> The sauce was announced to return to all McDonald's stores on February 26, 2018, due to popular demand from ''Rick and Morty'' fans.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://money.cnn.com/2017/10/09/news/companies/rick-and-morty-mcdonalds/index.html|title=McDonald's vows to reboot Szechuan Sauce for spurned 'Rick and Morty' fans|last1=Smith|first1=Aaron|date=October 9, 2017|work=CNN Money|access-date=December 15, 2017|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171215001154/http://money.cnn.com/2017/10/09/news/companies/rick-and-morty-mcdonalds/index.html|archive-date=December 15, 2017}}</ref>

On March 31, 2022, it once again returned to stores, featured as an app-only exclusive.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Tyko |first=Kelly |date=March 31, 2022 |title=McDonald's Szechuan Sauce is back. Here's how to get the McNuggets dipping sauce for free. |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/money/food/2022/03/31/szechuan-sauce-mcdonalds-2022/7231520001/ |access-date=September 28, 2022 |website=USA Today |language=en-US}}</ref>

On July 19, 2023, the sauce returned to New Zealand for a limited time to promote the [[2023 FIFA Women's World Cup]].<ref>{{Cite web|date=July 19, 2023|title=McDonald's NZ releases rare Szechuan Sauce for limited time|access-date=January 14, 2025|url=https://www.nzherald.co.nz/lifestyle/mcdonalds-nz-releases-rare-szechuan-sauce-for-limited-time/LO7OH3B5DVDDFLN3A3EJ7PZPWQ/|language=en-NZ|website=[[The New Zealand Herald]] }}</ref>

On June 25, 2024, it returned to Canadian stores, for a promotional campaign called ''Throwback Sauces''.<ref>{{Cite web |date=June 24, 2024 |title=McNugget Lovers: Dip into three flavours of McDonald's nostalgia with the new Throwback Sauces |url=https://www.mcdonalds.com/ca/en-ca/newsroom/article/McNugget-Lovers--Dip-into-Three-Flavours-of-McDonald-s-Nostalgia---with-the-new-Throwback-Sauces.html |access-date=June 24, 2024 |website=McDonald's |language=en-CA}}</ref>

On July 23, 2024, McDonald's France released a campaign for the Olympics called ''"Croquez le monde"'' (Bite the world), which offered re-issues of seven iconic products, including the Szechuan Sauce. However, customers said that it had different ingredients and taste compared to the US version.<ref>{{Cite web |last=à 12h41 |first=Par Hadrien Gonzales Le 5 août 2024 |date=August 5, 2024 |title=VIDÉO. JO Paris 2024 : la « fausse » sauce szechuan de McDonald's |url=https://www.leparisien.fr/bien-manger/video-la-fausse-sauce-szechuan-de-mcdonalds-05-08-2024-RGDUR3OD7NCX5DPF4LVRVZ7VRQ.php |access-date=August 6, 2024 |website=leparisien.fr |language=fr-FR}}</ref>

